@startuml HU13_RBAC_secuencia
title HU-13 — RBAC: roles y autorización\nAuthorization middleware (Chain of Responsibility)

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2E75B6
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EBF3FB
skinparam noteBorderColor #F0A500
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1

actor       "Cliente (rol X)"                  as Client
boundary    "Frontend (React)"                 as UI
participant "rateLimiter\n(>100 req/min => 429)" as RL
participant "protect (JWT)"                     as PRT
participant "authorize(...roles)"              as AUTH
control     "Controller protegido\n(p.ej. loanController.liquidate)" as CTL
database    "PostgreSQL (users)"               as DB

autonumber

note over RL, AUTH
  Chain of Responsibility: rateLimiter -> protect -> authorize(...roles) -> handler.
  Cada eslabón corta la cadena con su propio status (429 / 401 / 403) o llama next().
  User.role in {borrower, lender, admin}.
end note

Client -> UI : Acción sensible (p.ej. liquidar / PATCH role / GET metrics)
UI -> RL : request (JWT)
activate RL
alt supera límite de tasa
    RL --> UI : 429 Too Many Requests
else dentro del límite
    RL -> PRT : next()
    deactivate RL
    activate PRT
    alt sin token / token inválido
        PRT --> UI : 401 Unauthorized
    else token válido
        PRT -> DB : User.findByPk(decoded.id)
        DB --> PRT : req.user (con role)
        PRT -> AUTH : next()
        deactivate PRT
        activate AUTH
        alt req.user.role NO está en roles permitidos
            AUTH -> AUTH : log intento no autorizado
            AUTH --> UI : 403 Forbidden (registrado)
        else rol autorizado
            AUTH -> CTL : next()
            deactivate AUTH
            activate CTL
            CTL --> UI : 200 / 201 (operación ejecutada)
            deactivate CTL
        end
    end
end

== Cambio de rol (solo admin) ==
UI -> AUTH : PATCH /api/users/{id}/role { role } (JWT admin)
AUTH -> CTL : authController.updateRole
CTL -> DB : User.update({ role } where id)
DB --> CTL : OK
CTL --> UI : 200 { user }

note over Client, DB
  Endpoints protegidos por authorize('admin'): liquidación manual (HU-09),
  /api/metrics (HU-14), PATCH role (HU-13). QA: rbac.test.js
  (200 con rol correcto, 403 rol insuficiente, 401 sin token).
  Escenario de calidad 4 (RBAC).
end note

@enduml
